  "body": "## Why\n\n4.26.0 reduced `fcc-claude` to the two proxy variables, which dropped `CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY`. Measured against a live proxy, that variable is exactly what makes Claude Code fetch the catalog:\n\n```\nfcc-claude       GET /health,                          POST /v1/messages\nfcc-claude-old   GET /health, GET /v1/models?limit=1000, POST /v1/messages\n```\n\nSo the native `/model` picker stopped listing FCC's models under the default launcher. Requests still routed correctly — only the picker was affected.\n\n## What this does\n\nAdds an FCC-only `--discover-models` flag to `fcc-claude`:\n\n```bash\nfcc-claude --discover-models\n```\n\n- Stripped from argv **before Claude Code sees it**, and only when it appears before a bare `--` separator, so a literal occurrence inside a passed-through prompt survives.\n- The minimal default is **unchanged**. The catalog fetch is an extra request to the proxy on every launch, which is why this is opt-in rather than simply restored.\n- `build_minimal_claude_proxy_env` grows a keyword-only `enable_model_discovery` parameter rather than a third builder. `fcc-claude-old` is untouched.\n\n## The documentation half — arguably the more important one\n\nThe README feature table claimed *\"each agent's native model picker works against the FCC catalog\"*. That became **false for `fcc-claude`** the moment 4.26.0 shipped. The same claim appeared in five more places. All corrected to state which launcher they apply to:\n\n| File | Claim fixed |\n| --- | --- |\n| `README.md` | feature table, screenshot caption, \"Connect Claude Code\" intro, launcher section |\n| `docs/USAGE.md` | \"three consequences\" list, Step 4 + caption, Shortcut section |\n| `admin_static/index.html` | guide \"how it works\" list, Claude Code step 4, hand-edit fallback |\n\n**Codex and Pi are genuinely unaffected**, and the docs still say so — verified against the code, not assumed: `codex.py` fetches the proxy model list and builds a catalog of its own, and `pi.py` passes `--models`.\n\nThe **settings.json route has the same gap**, so the manual instructions and the guide's hand-edit fallback now mention adding `\"CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY\": \"1\"` to the same `env` block.\n\n## Verification\n\nLive measurement against a 4.27.0 server, requests attributed by log-line boundaries:\n\n```\n=== fcc-claude (no flag) ===\n\"GET /health\"\n\"POST /v1/messages?beta=true\"\n\n=== fcc-claude --discover-models ===\n\"GET /health\"\n\"GET /v1/models?limit=1000\"\n\"POST /v1/messages?beta=true\"\n```\n\nBoth runs completed a real prompt, which also proves the flag never reaches the `claude` binary — an unknown argument would have aborted it.\n\n**Full suite: 3169 passed, 14 failed** — the documented pre-existing baseline (8 defeated by real API keys in the shell environment, 6 PowerShell installer tests), unchanged on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **The 4.26.0 dashboard card still writes only the two keys**, so configuring through the button leaves the picker empty as well. Documented, not fixed — whether that card should offer the discovery key is a product decision rather than part of this change.\n- The argv rule means a bare `--discover-models` in the leading section is always treated as our flag. Documented in the helper's docstring. A prompt needing that literal text can put it after `--`.\n- The picker itself was confirmed only through the proxy's access log, not by eye in an interactive session.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
