    "committer": {
     "name": "Contributor",
     "email": "dev@example.com",
     "date": "2026-08-06T16:02:19Z"
    },
    "message": "feat(cli): opt into Claude Code's model picker with --discover-models\n\n4.26.0 reduced fcc-claude to the two proxy variables, which removed\nCLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY. Measured against a live proxy,\nthat variable is exactly what makes Claude Code fetch the catalog:\n\n    fcc-claude       GET /health,                      POST /v1/messages\n    fcc-claude-old   GET /health, GET /v1/models?...,  POST /v1/messages\n\nSo the native /model picker stopped listing FCC's models under the default\nlauncher. Requests still routed correctly; only the picker was affected.\n\nAdds an FCC-only --discover-models flag to fcc-claude. It is stripped from\nargv before Claude Code sees it, and only when it appears before a bare `--`\nseparator, so a literal occurrence in a passed-through prompt survives. The\nminimal default is unchanged: the catalog fetch is an extra request to the\nproxy on every launch, which is why it is opt-in rather than restored.\nbuild_minimal_claude_proxy_env grows a keyword-only enable_model_discovery\nparameter rather than a third builder. fcc-claude-old is untouched.\n\nThe larger half of this change is documentation. The README feature table\nclaimed \"each agent's native model picker works against the FCC catalog\",\nwhich became false for fcc-claude the moment 4.26.0 shipped. The same claim\nappeared in the README screenshot caption and connect section, in\ndocs/USAGE.md twice, and in the in-dashboard guide. Each now states which\nlauncher it applies to. Codex and Pi are unaffected and still say so:\ncodex.py fetches the proxy model list and builds a catalog of its own, and\npi.py passes --models.\n\nThe settings.json route has the same gap, so the manual instructions and the\nguide's hand-edit fallback now mention adding\n\"CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_GATEWAY_MODEL_DISCOVERY\": \"1\" to the same env block.\n\nVerification:\n- Live measurement against a 4.27.0 server. With the flag, GET\n  /v1/models?limit=1000 appears; without it, absent. Both runs completed a\n  real prompt, which also proves the flag never reaches the claude binary --\n  an unknown argument would have aborted it.\n- Full suite: 3169 passed, 14 failed -- the documented pre-existing baseline\n  (8 defeated by real API keys in the shell environment, 6 PowerShell\n  installer tests), unchanged on unmodified main.\n\nNot done: the 4.26.0 dashboard card still writes only the two keys, so\nconfiguring through the button leaves the picker empty too. Whether that card\nshould offer the discovery key is a product decision, not part of this change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
